<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Holland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806–1810</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Holland was a monarchy created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in 1806 to replace the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a>, with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-bonaparte">Louis Bonaparte</a> as king. Louis tried to protect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> interests, enforcing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a> only loosely, and he sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herman-willem-daendels">Herman Willem Daendels</a> to govern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Displeased, Napoleon forced Louis to abdicate in 1810 and annexed the kingdom to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p></div>
